# Artificial Neural Networks in Policy Research: A Current Assessment.

**Authors:** Woelfel, Joseph

## Abstract
Suggests that artificial neural networks (ANNs) exhibit properties that promise usefulness for policy researchers. Notes that ANNs have found extensive use in areas once reserved for multivariate statistical programs such as regression and multiple classification analysis and are developing an extensive community of advocates for processing text and other qualitative information. (RS)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ459304

